      "writtenOn": "2022-01-05T14:27:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that\u0027s only possible right now because the late-bound \"content\" image happens to be equivalent to \u0027image\u0027 since that\u0027s all that is drawn to the layer. Additionally, the current API only lets you have one such bind target that can be set to an image filter. This new API lets you have N image filters as children, and automatically late-binds their evaluated images as children to the program (so roughly equivalent to makeShader() except the image isn\u0027t known until the filter is executed).",
